# CanonSim Workbench — strings.gd, the single translation boundary (ux-1).
#
# FRONTEND_UIUX_LAW §17: ONE boundary — `_tr()` keys over every user-facing
# GDScript string; localization-READY layout (Cyrillic-safe metrics,
# wrapping, long-label tolerance), never hard-coded literals in surface
# code. The catalogs carry the EN values the shell previously inlined
# (the migration is literal-exact: the EN entry IS the old literal) and
# the RU companion (the owner's language; resolved by OS locale, the
# --lang user arg, or the CANONSIM_LANG env — see shell.gd _resolve_locale).
#
# The NOT-localized set (kept literal in shell.gd by law):
#   · protocol/contract values — model lifecycle states (DISCOVERED /
#     ACTIVE / SELECTED / EVICTED / LOADING / UNLOADING / FAILED), the
#     fa forms (on/off/auto), wire names (chat.send, run.get, …) — the
#     canonical vocabulary is displayed verbatim, never re-worded
#   · the authority vocabulary line (CANONICAL · OBSERVED · DERIVED ·
#     UNKNOWN · HIDDEN · VISUAL) — terms, not prose
#   · byte-size formats (GB/MB/B) — locale-neutral units
#
# Proof mode pins locale "en" (the byte-identical capture law, §22).
